cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Delayed non-reciprocal Hopfield networks: code, data and evidence for the
  quenched bifurcation ensemble
message: >-
  If you use this software or data, please cite it using the metadata from this
  file. The accompanying manuscript is in preparation.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Flack
    given-names: L.
abstract: >-
  Code, derived data and a claim-by-claim evidence register for the study of
  sequential memory recall in delayed non-reciprocal Hopfield networks. The work
  resolves, inside a single disordered sample, the ensemble of quenched
  saddle-node bifurcations at which stored memories lose stability, and shows
  that two distinct macroscopic phase boundaries are two different order
  statistics of that one internal law.
keywords:
  - Hopfield network
  - non-reciprocal dynamics
  - delay differential equations
  - saddle-node bifurcation
  - extreme value statistics
  - finite-size effects
  - disordered systems
  - hyperchaos
  - sequential memory
license: MIT
